# Key layout for the Amazon Fire TV remote (HID product id 0x042F, "AR")
# used with the Fire TV Stick Lite / 3rd Gen (sheldon / sheldonp).
#
# The remote reports its select key as HID usage 0x58 (KEY_KPENTER). The generic
# key layout maps key 96 to NUMPAD_ENTER, and Android only opens the soft
# keyboard for DPAD_CENTER / ENTER (TextView.onKeyUp), so text fields - search,
# Wi-Fi password, logins - could not be activated with the OK button of the
# remote. With DPAD_CENTER the on-screen keyboard appears as expected.
#
# Everything else matches the other Amazon BLE remote layouts in this directory
# (see Vendor_0171_Product_0412/0415/041e/041f.kl); the key set below is the
# union of those, so no key of this remote is left unmapped.

key 116   TV_POWER
key 217   SEARCH

key 96    DPAD_CENTER
key 103   DPAD_UP
key 105   DPAD_LEFT
key 106   DPAD_RIGHT
key 108   DPAD_DOWN

key 172   HOME
key 158   BACK
key 139   MENU

key 113   VOLUME_MUTE
key 114   VOLUME_DOWN
key 115   VOLUME_UP

key 168   MEDIA_REWIND
key 208   MEDIA_FAST_FORWARD
key 164   MEDIA_PLAY_PAUSE

key 362   TV

# App keys (Prime Video, Netflix, Apps, Amazon Music).
# Note: on product 0x042F these four buttons are delivered as HID consumer
# reports (report id 0xEF) and never reach the input stack, so the key codes
# below only apply if a firmware revision maps them to real key events.
key 744   BUTTON_1    WAKE
key 745   BUTTON_2    WAKE
key 746   ALL_APPS    WAKE
key 747   BUTTON_5    WAKE
